{
  "id": "Compound::DB00294 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Etonogestrel is linked to Cyp3a4 through a series of molecular interactions, primarily through its inclusion in the Progesterone Congeners class, which includes Norethindrone. This class is known to bind to Cyp3a4, suggesting a potential role in drug metabolism. The lowest common ancestor of Etonogestrel and Norethindrone is the 3-Oxo-Delta(4) Steroid, indicating a shared structural foundation that may facilitate interaction with Cyp3a4. Additionally, Etonogestrel's ability to cause Pelvic Discomfort and Genital Discharge, which are both linked to Norethindrone, further supports a pathway where Norethindrone's interaction with Cyp3a4 is mediated through Etonogestrel. The evidence suggests that Etonogestrel may act as a modulator or co-factor in the metabolic pathway involving Cyp3a4, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
